{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:91d1fd18fe2bb508","name":"ILH-KK Citadel-Class Civilian Cruiser","source":{"id":"source:reference-91d1fd18fe2bb508","title":"ILH-KK Citadel-Class Civilian Cruiser","revision":24261,"timestamp":"2024-10-29T15:02:47Z","sha256":"4632da1f69bd3afe844fa3a7ecef8b4c0ebe87d01021088de3590bba2b1d58b0","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24261","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=ILH-KK%20Citadel-Class%20Civilian%20Cruiser&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-91d1fd18fe2bb508","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Koensayr ILH-KK ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadel"]},"-Class Civilian Cruiser is a popular armed transport developed during the last years of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},". It's well regarded as a ship able to take a considerable pounding before failing, and many have been successfully rebuilt even after being virtually destroyed in battle. Designed as a response to increasing fears among the moderately wealthy that star travel was not safe, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadel"]}," peaked in popularity during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," and waned during the Galactic Civil War. Many were converted into luxury yachts, while others became minor warships for Rebels, freebooters, the CSA, and pirates.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Designed for those who can afford a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," but not a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},", the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadel"]},"-Class Cruiser is geared for small groups traveling together. It is popular with small diplomatic parties, wealthy merchants, mid-level military officers, and galactic adventurers. The ships are so durable that most go through many owners and many different intended uses. As a result, it is not unusual to find one with a mix of tacked-on military hardware, a few smuggling compartments, a diplomatic council room, and fading murals painted on the bulkheads.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The factory-installed weapons of the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadel"]}," are largely defensive in nature. ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadels"]}," also have two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Docking Clamps"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Docking_Clamps","referenceId":"reference:b4a9e9f91fcb2a40"}," used as external fighter mountings attached to the ships' undersides. This feature allows the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadel"]}," to carry ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," that lack ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrives"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrives"}," of their own through hyperspace. Military groups working on a budget and some pirate groups have used this potential to create small fleets of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadels"]}," carrying ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," or similar craft on deep-space missions.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["ILH-KK ",{"tag":"i","children":["Citadel"]},"-Class Civilian Cruiser Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org